  </data>
  <data name="help_helper_tagline" xml:space="preserve">
    <value>Bring browser history into HistoryLib.</value>
  </data>
  <data name="help_helper_description" xml:space="preserve">
    <value>HistoryLib Helper is a separate local-only tool for Windows and macOS. It reads supported browser history and exports a .hlz file that HistoryLib can import.</value>
  </data>
  <data name="help_supported_browsers_title" xml:space="preserve">
    <value>Supported Browsers</value>
  </data>
  <data name="help_supported_browsers_body" xml:space="preserve">
    <value>Google Chrome, Microsoft Edge, Brave, Vivaldi, Opera, Chromium, and Firefox are supported.</value>
  </data>
  <data name="help_import_options_title" xml:space="preserve">
    <value>Import Options</value>
  </data>
  <data name="help_import_options_body_1" xml:space="preserve">
    <value>HistoryLib can directly import only Safari history, Google Takeout exports, and .hlz archives.</value>
  </data>
  <data name="help_import_options_body_2" xml:space="preserve">
    <value>To import history from a computer or from more browsers, use HistoryLib Helper to create a .hlz archive, then import that archive into HistoryLib.</value>
  </data>
  <data name="help_how_it_works_title" xml:space="preserve">
